---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base>
  <header class="bar">
    <div class="wrap bar-in">
      <span class="wordmark">shulian<span class="dot">.</span>dev</span>
      <nav class="top">
        <a href="#work" class="nav-hide">Work</a>
        <a href="#stack" class="nav-hide">Stack</a>
        <a href="#path" class="nav-hide">Path</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
        <button class="theme-btn" id="themeBtn" type="button" aria-label="Toggle color theme">◑ theme</button>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="wrap">
    <section class="hero" id="top">
      <h1>Julián Antonucci</h1>
      <p class="role">
        Senior backend engineer building <b>Node.js</b> services that stay predictable under load —
        <b>distributed systems</b>, <b>Postgres</b>, and pragmatic <b>AWS</b>.
      </p>

      <div class="facts">
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="k mono">Now</div>
          <div class="v">
            Lead backend on <a href="#work">ink-cover</a> — migrating the platform from a DigitalOcean
            droplet to AWS serverless, zero downtime.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="k mono">Stack</div>
          <div class="v mono">Node.js · TypeScript · Postgres · TypeORM · AWS (Lambda · SQS · S3 · CloudFront)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="k mono">Based</div>
          <div class="v">Argentina · working remote across time zones</div>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="k mono">Links</div>
          <div class="v">
            <a href="https://github.com/JulianNicolas">GitHub</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp;
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/julian-antonucci/">LinkedIn</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp;
            <a href="#contact">CV (PDF)</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp;
            <a href="mailto:antonuccijulian@gmail.com">Email</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="work">
      <p class="eyebrow">Selected work</p>

      <!-- CASE 1 — real -->
      <article class="case">
        <div class="case-body">
          <div class="case-head">
            <h3>ink-cover — serverless migration</h3>
            <span class="when mono">2025 – present</span>
          </div>
          <p class="lede">
            A Node.js/TypeScript product that turns uploaded images into analysis reports. I lead the
            backend and I'm moving the whole platform off one droplet onto AWS serverless while it
            keeps serving traffic.
          </p>

          <h4>Where it started</h4>
          <p class="para">
            A single DigitalOcean droplet ran the API, the Postgres database and image processing
            together. Deploys were a <code>git push</code> that SSH'd into the box — no CI gate, no
            rollback, no preview. Every upload processed synchronously, so traffic spikes queued
            behind image work and the API slowed for everyone.
          </p>

          <div
            class="arch"
            role="img"
            aria-label="Architecture before and after: a single droplet running API, Postgres and image processing becomes CloudFront in front of a Lambda API that enqueues work on SQS for a worker Lambda, with S3 for bytes and managed Postgres."
          >
            <div class="arch-grid">
              <div class="arch-col before">
                <h5>Before</h5>
                <div class="flow">
                  <div class="node">client</div>
                  <div class="link-v"></div>
                  <div class="node hot">1× droplet<br />API + Postgres + image proc</div>
                  <div class="link-v"></div>
                  <div class="node hot">base64 blobs in DB</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="arch-col after">
                <h5>After</h5>
                <div class="flow">
                  <div class="node">client</div>
                  <div class="link-v"></div>
                  <div class="node">CloudFront</div>
                  <div class="link-v"></div>
                  <div class="node key">API · Lambda</div>
                  <div class="link-v"></div>
                  <div class="split">
                    <div class="node key">SQS → worker</div>
                    <div class="node">Postgres</div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="link-v"></div>
                  <div class="node key">S3 · image + preview bytes</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h4>What I did</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Introduced a <code>StoragePort</code> interface with an <code>S3Storage</code>
              implementation, moving image and preview bytes out of Postgres and onto S3. Read paths
              now serve signed URLs instead of base64 payloads.
            </li>
            <li>
              Added <code>previewKey</code> / <code>imageKey</code> columns plus a backfill, and
              relaxed the legacy <code>base64 NOT NULL</code> constraint so old and new rows coexist
              through the cutover.
            </li>
            <li>
              Redesigned the analysis pipeline around a queue: uploads return immediately, processing
              runs on a worker that scales independently of the API.
            </li>
            <li>
              Killed a class of "stale app after deploy" bugs — a cached <code>index.html</code> and
              orphaned service workers that kept serving a months-old bundle to returning users.
            </li>
            <li>
              Next: CI gate + preview environments in front of the auto-deploy pipeline, so a push
              can't ship a broken build straight to production.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <aside class="panel">
          <div class="panel-card">
            <div class="panel-row">
              <span class="m-k mono">Impact</span>
              <span class="m-v">Zero-downtime cutover, in progress</span>
            </div>
            <div class="panel-row">
              <span class="m-k mono">Upload p95</span>
              <span class="m-v slot mono">sync → async · add metric</span>
            </div>
            <div class="panel-row">
              <span class="m-k mono">Infra cost / mo</span>
              <span class="m-v slot mono">DO $XX <span class="arrow">→</span> AWS $YY</span>
            </div>
            <div class="panel-row">
              <span class="m-k mono">Deploy safety</span>
              <span class="m-v">manual SSH <span class="arrow">→</span> CI + preview</span>
            </div>
            <div class="panel-row">
              <span class="m-k mono">Role</span>
              <span class="m-v">Lead backend engineer</span>
            </div>
            <div class="stacklist">
              <span class="chip">Node.js</span><span class="chip">TypeScript</span><span class="chip">TypeORM</span>
              <span class="chip">Postgres</span><span class="chip">AWS S3</span><span class="chip">SQS</span>
              <span class="chip">Lambda</span><span class="chip">CloudFront</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </article>

      <!-- CASE 2 — template -->
      <article class="case">
        <div class="case-body">
          <div class="case-head">
            <h3>High-throughput ingestion API</h3>
            <span class="when mono">20XX – 20XX</span>
            <span class="tag">Template — replace with your project</span>
          </div>
          <p class="lede">
            One paragraph: the product, the load it takes, and the one hard constraint that shaped
            the design (a latency budget, an ordering guarantee, a cost ceiling).
          </p>
          <h4>What I did</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>The architectural decision you'd defend in an interview — and the trade-off you accepted to make it.</li>
            <li>A reliability or data-integrity problem you found and fixed.</li>
            <li>A performance change with a before/after number in the panel.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <aside class="panel">
          <div class="panel-card">
            <div class="panel-row"><span class="m-k mono">Throughput</span><span class="m-v slot mono">X req/s sustained</span></div>
            <div class="panel-row"><span class="m-k mono">p99 latency</span><span class="m-v slot mono">Xms → Yms</span></div>
            <div class="panel-row"><span class="m-k mono">Team</span><span class="m-v slot mono">size · your role</span></div>
            <div class="stacklist">
              <span class="chip">Node.js</span><span class="chip">Kafka / SQS</span><span class="chip">Redis</span><span class="chip">Postgres</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </article>

      <!-- CASE 3 — template -->
      <article class="case">
        <div class="case-body">
          <div class="case-head">
            <h3>Payments &amp; billing service</h3>
            <span class="when mono">20XX – 20XX</span>
            <span class="tag">Template — replace with your project</span>
          </div>
          <p class="lede">
            A domain where correctness matters more than speed — money, subscriptions, entitlements.
            Say what "wrong" would have cost.
          </p>
          <h4>What I did</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>How you made operations idempotent and safe to retry.</li>
            <li>How you reconciled against the provider (Stripe, MercadoPago) and caught drift.</li>
            <li>An audit or observability practice you introduced.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <aside class="panel">
          <div class="panel-card">
            <div class="panel-row"><span class="m-k mono">Volume</span><span class="m-v slot mono">$ / month processed</span></div>
            <div class="panel-row"><span class="m-k mono">Reconciliation</span><span class="m-v slot mono">mismatch rate</span></div>
            <div class="stacklist">
              <span class="chip">Node.js</span><span class="chip">TypeScript</span><span class="chip">Stripe</span><span class="chip">Postgres</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </article>

      <p class="note">
        Case 1 is drawn from real work on this project. Cases 2 and 3 are structural templates — same
        shape, your projects and numbers. Three deep case studies read better than a grid of ten repos.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="stack">
      <p class="eyebrow">Stack</p>
      <div class="stack-grid">
        <div class="stack-col">
          <h3>Runtime</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Node.js <span>— core</span></li>
            <li>TypeScript <span>— strict</span></li>
            <li>NestJS / Express</li>
            <li>Vitest · Jest</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="stack-col">
          <h3>Data</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>PostgreSQL <span>— primary</span></li>
            <li>TypeORM · Prisma</li>
            <li>Redis <span>— cache · locks</span></li>
            <li>SQL modelling · migrations</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="stack-col">
          <h3>AWS</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Lambda · API Gateway</li>
            <li>SQS · EventBridge</li>
            <li>S3 · CloudFront</li>
            <li>RDS · IAM · CDK</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="stack-col">
          <h3>Delivery</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Docker</li>
            <li>GitHub Actions <span>— CI/CD</span></li>
            <li>Observability <span>— logs · traces</span></li>
            <li>Load &amp; failure testing</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="path">
      <p class="eyebrow">Path</p>
      <div class="path">
        <div class="stop">
          <div class="yr">2025 — now</div>
          <div class="role">
            <b>Lead Backend Engineer</b> · <span class="co">ink-cover</span>
            <p>
              Own the backend. Leading the DigitalOcean → AWS serverless migration; storage
              abstraction, queue-based pipeline, deploy safety.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="stop">
          <div class="yr">20XX — 20XX</div>
          <div class="role">
            <b>Senior Backend Engineer</b> · <span class="co">Company</span>
            <p class="tag inline">Template — one line on scope, scale, and what you owned.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="stop">
          <div class="yr">20XX — 20XX</div>
          <div class="role">
            <b>Backend Engineer</b> · <span class="co">Company</span>
            <p>Template — the role where you went from "writes features" to "owns systems".</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
      <p class="contact-lead">
        Hiring for a backend or platform role, or need a system that won't fall over? <b>Let's talk.</b>
      </p>
      <div class="clinks">
        <a class="clink" href="mailto:antonuccijulian@gmail.com">✉ <span class="mono">antonuccijulian@gmail.com</span></a>
        <a class="clink" href="https://github.com/JulianNicolas">⌥ <span class="mono">github.com/JulianNicolas</span></a>
        <a class="clink" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/julian-antonucci/">in <span class="mono">linkedin.com/in/julian-antonucci</span></a>
        <a class="clink" href="#">↓ <span class="mono">Résumé — PDF</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div class="wrap foot-in">
      <span>© 2026 Julián Antonucci — shulian.dev</span>
      <span class="mono">Built with Astro · deployed on Vercel</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var btn = document.getElementById('themeBtn');
      var root = document.documentElement;
      function current() {
        var t = root.getAttribute('data-theme');
        if (t) return t;
        return window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light';
      }
      btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        var next = current() === 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark';
        root.setAttribute('data-theme', next);
        try {
          localStorage.setItem('shulian-theme', next);
        } catch (e) {}
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  /* ---------- tokens: light (bare :root = full palette) ---------- */
  :root {
    --ground: #f4f5f8;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --surface-sunk: #edeff3;
    --ink: #14181f;
    --ink-soft: #3b434f;
    --muted: #626c7a;
    --hairline: #dce0e8;
    --hairline-2: #c9cfda;
    --accent: #1e5fcc;
    --accent-ink: #17408a;
    --good: #1c8f63;
    --warn: #b3730e;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(20, 24, 31, 0.05), 0 8px 28px -12px rgba(20, 24, 31, 0.14);
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme='light']) {
      --ground: #0e1116;
      --surface: #151a21;
      --surface-sunk: #11151b;
      --ink: #e8ebf1;
      --ink-soft: #c2c9d4;
      --muted: #8c97a6;
      --hairline: #262c36;
      --hairline-2: #333b47;
      --accent: #6098f6;
      --accent-ink: #a9c6fb;
      --good: #3fb784;
      --warn: #d69537;
      --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4), 0 12px 34px -14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
    }
  }
  :root[data-theme='dark'] {
    --ground: #0e1116;
    --surface: #151a21;
    --surface-sunk: #11151b;
    --ink: #e8ebf1;
    --ink-soft: #c2c9d4;
    --muted: #8c97a6;
    --hairline: #262c36;
    --hairline-2: #333b47;
    --accent: #6098f6;
    --accent-ink: #a9c6fb;
    --good: #3fb784;
    --warn: #d69537;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4), 0 12px 34px -14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
  }

  *,
  *::before,
  *::after {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  html {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
    -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
  }
  img,
  svg {
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    html {
      scroll-behavior: auto;
    }
    * {
      transition: none !important;
      animation: none !important;
    }
  }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--ground);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.65;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  .mono {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  :focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 3px;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  .wrap {
    max-width: 1060px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 28px;
  }

  /* ---------- top bar ---------- */
  header.bar {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 20;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ground) 86%, transparent);
    backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .bar-in {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    height: 54px;
  }
  .wordmark {
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .wordmark .dot {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  nav.top {
    display: flex;
    gap: 22px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  nav.top a {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }
  nav.top a:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .theme-btn {
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline-2);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 4px 9px;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .theme-btn:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    nav.top a.nav-hide {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  /* ---------- eyebrow ---------- */
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 500;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 0 0 26px;
  }
  .eyebrow::after {
    content: '';
    flex: 1;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--hairline);
  }

  section {
    padding: 68px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  main.wrap > section:first-of-type {
    border-top: 0;
  }

  /* ---------- hero ---------- */
  .hero {
    padding: 74px 0 60px;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 3.7rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.04;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .hero .role {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.4vw, 1.3rem);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-weight: 300;
    margin: 0 0 34px;
    max-width: 34ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .hero .role b {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .facts {
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--surface);
    overflow: hidden;
    max-width: 620px;
  }
  .fact {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 92px 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
  }
  .fact:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
  }
  .fact .k {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding-top: 3px;
  }
  .fact .v {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .fact .v a {
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* ---------- case studies ---------- */
  .case {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 30px;
  }
  .case + .case {
    margin-top: 30px;
    padding-top: 46px;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--hairline-2);
  }
  @media (min-width: 860px) {
    .case {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 292px;
      gap: 44px;
    }
  }

  .case-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 10px 14px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .case h3 {
    font-size: 1.42rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .case .when {
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .tag {
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 500;
    padding: 3px 7px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--warn);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 40%, var(--hairline));
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 9%, transparent);
  }
  .tag.inline {
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .case .lede {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 4px 0 20px;
  }
  .case .para {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.94rem;
  }
  .case h4 {
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.13em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 22px 0 10px;
  }
  .case ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .case ul li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 20px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.94rem;
  }
  .case ul li::before {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
  }
  .case code {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.84em;
    background: var(--surface-sunk);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .panel {
    align-self: start;
  }
  @media (min-width: 860px) {
    .panel {
      position: sticky;
      top: 74px;
    }
  }
  .panel-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--surface);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .panel-row {
    padding: 11px 15px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    display: grid;
    gap: 3px;
  }
  .panel-row:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
    background: var(--surface-sunk);
  }
  .panel-row .m-k {
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .panel-row .m-v {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink);
